---
layout: base.njk
description: "Give it your website. Prospektor finds the companies worth approaching, names who to write to, and writes the pitch in your voice."
# One page per language the build knows (#114): `/` in English, `/es/` and so
# on for every catalogue under src/_data/strings/. Every sentence below sits
# in a {% t %} block and renders untouched on the English page; the pagination
# is what makes the other languages exist at all. Nothing here lists them.
pagination:
  data: languages
  size: 1
  alias: language
  addAllPagesToCollections: true
permalink: "{{ language.prefix }}/"
---

{#- The homepage in the studio's look (#1092, 7 Oct 2026): the grey ground,
    white cards with no border and no shadow, and coral on exactly one press,
    the scan field's. Below the hero, four tiles name what the product does
    in short lines (since #1279), and the two product pages carry the studio's own names
    for its screens. The five agents, the six-stage run card and the batch
    band are gone with the run model they described.

    The operator on the draft: "keep it minimal and clean. I want the primary
    CTA still to be clearly to scan the site and not immediately go into
    product screenshots." So the hero is the promise, one sentence, the field
    and one quiet line to the demo, and nothing else.

    #207: the anchor is the SECTION, not the field inside it. Every "Scan your
    site" on this site is a /#scan jump; the hero is the first thing in the
    document, so the target resolves to scroll 0 and the headline and the
    field arrive together. test/drive.js §6b measures it. -#}
<section class="hero" id="scan">
  {#- .hero-rest collapses when a scan starts (scan.js adds .scan-focus to
      the hero): from that moment the scan is the page. -#}
  <div class="hero-rest" id="heroRest">
    {#- #453: the h1 carries the words the <title> shows (site.tagline), and
        test/pages.test.js holds the two together. -#}
    <h1>{% t %}Find Leads.<br><span class="accent">That fit you.</span>{% endt %}</h1>
    <p class="hero-sub">{% t %}Give it your website. It finds the companies worth approaching and writes the pitch in your voice.{% endt %}</p>
  </div>

  <!-- The scan field: POST /api/scan, poll, render the proposal. scan.js drives it. -->
  <div class="scan-hero">
    <form class="scan-form" id="scanForm" novalidate>
      <div class="scan-q">
        <svg class="scan-q-icon" width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"></circle><path d="M20 20l-3.5-3.5"></path></svg>
        {#- #241: the field is a combobox over #scanSuggest; the browser's own
            URL autofill is off so it cannot draw a second list over ours. -#}
        <input class="scan-input" id="scanInput" type="text" inputmode="url" autocomplete="off"
               role="combobox" aria-autocomplete="list" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="scanSuggest"
               spellcheck="false" placeholder="yourcompany.com" aria-label="{% t %}Your company website{% endt %}">
      </div>
      <button class="scan-btn" type="submit" id="scanBtn">{% t %}Find my leads{% endt %}</button>
      {#- #241: companies matching what has been typed, one line each (name,
          domain), written by scan.js from the site's own company-suggest
          function. Picking one fills the field; nothing else moves. -#}
      <ul class="scan-suggest" id="scanSuggest" role="listbox" hidden></ul>
    </form>
    {#- The hint and the demo's door (#767) read as one line under the field.
        The door is a link and never a second button (style rule 8), and it
        goes with the rest of the hero the moment a scan starts. -#}
    <div class="scan-hints">
      <p class="scan-hint" id="scanHint">{% t %}Free, no sign-up, about 30 seconds.{% endt %}</p>
      <p class="scan-demo" id="scanDemo"><a href="{{ '/demo/' | localize }}">{% t %}Or click through the demo.{% endt %}</a></p>
    </div>
    <p class="scan-error" id="scanError" hidden></p>

    <div aria-live="polite">
      <div class="scan-status" id="scanStatus" hidden>
        <div class="scan-progress"><div class="scan-progress-fill" id="scanBarFill"></div></div>
        <div class="scan-status-line"><span class="building-dot"></span><span id="scanStatusMsg"></span></div>
      </div>

      {#- #240: one card, the exact width of the search bar above it. Name +
          domain, fact chips, the proposal: that's the whole result. -#}
      <div class="scan-result" id="scanResult" hidden>
        <div class="scan-card">
          <div class="scan-card-head">
            <span class="scan-card-name" id="scanName"></span>
            <span class="scan-card-domain" id="scanDomain"></span>
          </div>
          <div class="scan-chips" id="scanFacts" hidden></div>
          <p class="scan-lead">{% t %}Here's what Prospektor will find for you:{% endt %}</p>
          {#- Not a heading (#137): written by scan.js after the fetch returns. -#}
          <p class="scan-guess" id="scanGuess" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p>
          {#- #419: the free run is the primary action here, not checkout. The
              way to pay stays on the card as one quiet line, demoted and never
              removed, because the reader who is already sold must not have to
              hunt for it. -#}
          <div class="scan-cta-row">
            <a class="btn-cta" id="scanRunCta" href="https://studio.prospektor.ai/r">{% t %}Show me the companies →{% endt %}</a>
            <p class="scan-cta-note">{% t %}Free, no sign-up.{% endt %} <a id="scanCta" data-signup href="{{ site.studio }}/signup{% if language.code != 'en' %}?lang={{ language.code }}{% endif %}">{% t %}Start my studio →{% endt %}</a></p>
          </div>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="scan-fallback" id="scanFallback" hidden>
        <p class="scan-fallback-msg" id="scanFallbackMsg" hidden></p>
        <a class="btn-cta" id="scanFallbackCta" data-signup href="{{ site.studio }}/signup{% if language.code != 'en' %}?lang={{ language.code }}{% endif %}">{% t %}Start my studio →{% endt %}</a>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<script src="{{ '/assets/js/scan.js' | asset }}" defer></script>

{#- Below the hero, what you get (#1279, 13 Oct 2026, the operator's go on
    #1288): the Canada Post deck's slide 5 shape, four columns in the order a
    seller works, each a heading and two or three short lines of a name and
    what it does. It replaced #1185's four drawn tiles and ended their
    drawings-against-photos test; the photos stay on the two product pages.
    Every line is a live help article. Left out until each is true for a
    stranger: new Canadian companies, phone numbers, Salesforce, batch
    enrich. The whole column is the link into its product page. Keeps
    id="what" on the section and id="how" on the grid, so old deep links to
    either land here. -#}
<section class="sec home-sec" id="what">
  <div class="col">
    <div class="sec-h">
      <h2>{% t %}What you get{% endt %}</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="pcols" id="how">
      <a class="pcol" href="{{ '/who-to-pitch/' | localize }}">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="11" cy="11" r="7"/><path d="m20 20-4-4"/></svg>
        <h3>{% t %}Find the right companies{% endt %}</h3>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>{% t %}Lookalikes{% endt %}</dt><dd>{% t %}of your best customers{% endt %}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>{% t %}Competitors' customers{% endt %}</dt><dd>{% t %}who buys from a rival{% endt %}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>{% t %}Leads for you{% endt %}</dt><dd>{% t %}new fits, waiting when you log in{% endt %}</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </a>
      <a class="pcol" href="{{ '/who-to-pitch/' | localize }}#warm-intros">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="9" cy="8" r="3.5"/><path d="M2.5 20c.8-3.6 3.4-5.5 6.5-5.5s5.7 1.9 6.5 5.5"/><circle cx="17" cy="9" r="2.5"/><path d="M17 14c2.4 0 4 1.5 4.5 4"/></svg>
        <h3>{% t %}Reach the people who decide{% endt %}</h3>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>{% t %}Decision makers{% endt %}</dt><dd>{% t %}named, with their LinkedIn{% endt %}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>{% t %}Warm intros{% endt %}</dt><dd>{% t %}through people you know{% endt %}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>{% t %}Your CRM{% endt %}</dt><dd>{% t %}HubSpot, Attio or Close, one press{% endt %}</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </a>
      <a class="pcol" href="{{ '/what-to-send/' | localize }}">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 5h16v11H9l-5 4z"/><path d="M8 9h8M8 12h5"/></svg>
        <h3>{% t %}Know what to say{% endt %}</h3>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>{% t %}Research{% endt %}</dt><dd>{% t %}on any company, in fifteen seconds{% endt %}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>{% t %}The pitch{% endt %}</dt><dd>{% t %}email, deck and one-pager, in your voice{% endt %}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>{% t %}Call prep{% endt %}</dt><dd>{% t %}one page before every call{% endt %}</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </a>
      <a class="pcol" href="{{ '/what-to-send/' | localize }}#in-your-voice">
        <svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M9 18h6M10 21h4"/><path d="M12 3a6 6 0 0 0-3.5 10.9c.6.5 1 1.2 1 2.1h5c0-.9.4-1.6 1-2.1A6 6 0 0 0 12 3z"/></svg>
        <h3>{% t %}Sharper every pitch{% endt %}</h3>
        <dl>
          <div><dt>{% t %}Wins and losses{% endt %}</dt><dd>{% t %}shape the next pitch{% endt %}</dd></div>
          <div><dt>{% t %}Your edits{% endt %}</dt><dd>{% t %}teach it how you write{% endt %}</dd></div>
        </dl>
      </a>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>

{#- The thesis, priced. Keeps id="pricing": Stripe's cancel_url is /#pricing
    (test/checkout-session.test.js) and old deep links land here. #1097: the
    paid card's link opens the studio's sign-up, finished by signup.js. -#}
<section class="sec home-sec" id="pricing">
  <div class="col">
    <div class="sec-h">
      <h2>{% t %}Who to pitch is free{% endt %}</h2>
      <p>{% t %}What to send is one workspace, one price, your whole team in.{% endt %}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="grid2 price">
      <div class="hcard">
        <p class="hcard-q">{% t %}Who to pitch{% endt %}</p>
        <b class="big">{% t %}Free{% endt %}</b>
        <p class="per">{% t %}No card, no sign-up to start{% endt %}</p>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li>{% t %}Your site read, and what you should hunt for{% endt %}</li>
          <li>{% t %}Three companies that fit, scored{% endt %}</li>
          <li>{% t %}Who buys from one of your competitors{% endt %}</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="hcard-foot"><a href="#scan">{% t %}Scan your site{% endt %} ›</a></p>
      </div>
      <div class="hcard">
        <p class="hcard-q">{% t %}What to send{% endt %}</p>
        <b class="big">{% t %}$999 a month{% endt %}</b>
        <p class="per">{% t %}or $9,990 a year, two months free{% endt %}</p>
        <ul class="ticks">
          <li>{% t %}Every pitch: deck, one-pager, cold email, proposal{% endt %}</li>
          <li>{% t %}Warm intros from your network{% endt %}</li>
          <li>{% t %}Replies to inbound, and a sheet for every call{% endt %}</li>
          <li>{% t %}Your whole team, no seats to count{% endt %}</li>
        </ul>
        <p class="hcard-foot buy" id="buy"><a href="{{ site.studio }}/signup{% if language.code != 'en' %}?lang={{ language.code }}{% endif %}" id="buyLink" data-signup>{% t %}Start my studio →{% endt %}</a> <a class="quiet" href="{{ '/pricing/' | localize }}">{% t %}See pricing{% endt %} ›</a></p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<script src="{{ '/assets/js/signup.js' | asset }}" defer></script>

{#- Keep your CRM (#1396, 17 Nov 2026). The operator: "it becomes very
    clear that prospector sits on top of any CRM that you use and it's
    responsible for finding the right companies that fit the leads you're
    looking for and then feeding them into your CRM where you run your
    standardized sales process", in the shape of shootpick.com's how-it-works
    map. Where leads come from above (one tile per door the studio has, each a
    live help article), Prospektor as the one dark hub, the CRMs the studio
    connects below (the same seven as the integrations grid, each tile the door
    to its page), and a side panel that reads out the part under the pointer
    (flow.js). It replaced #838's row of chips, which said the same thing in
    one line. The vendors' marks are the directory's own files (#841). -#}
<section class="sec home-sec" id="crm">
  <div class="col">
    <div class="sec-h">
      <h2>{% t %}Keep your CRM.{% endt %}</h2>
      <p>{% t %}Prospektor finds the companies that fit and puts each one into the CRM you already run. Your pipeline, your stages and your follow-up stay where they are.{% endt %}</p>
    </div>
    <div class="flowmap" data-flowmap>
      <div class="fm">
        <p class="fm-cap">{% t %}Where leads come from{% endt %}</p>
        <div class="fm-row">
        <button type="button" class="fm-in" data-step="in"><span class="fm-ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="12" cy="12" r="9"/><path d="M3 12h18M12 3a14 14 0 0 1 0 18M12 3a14 14 0 0 0 0 18"/></svg></span><span class="fm-lbl">{% t %}Your website{% endt %}</span></button>
        <button type="button" class="fm-in" data-step="in"><span class="fm-ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="m12 3 2.7 5.6 6.1.8-4.5 4.3 1.1 6.1L12 17l-5.4 2.8 1.1-6.1L3.2 9.4l6.1-.8z"/></svg></span><span class="fm-lbl">{% t %}Your best customers{% endt %}</span></button>
        <button type="button" class="fm-in" data-step="in"><span class="fm-ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M5 21V4M5 4h12l-2 4 2 4H5"/></svg></span><span class="fm-lbl">{% t %}A competitor’s customers{% endt %}</span></button>
        <button type="button" class="fm-in" data-step="in"><span class="fm-ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><rect x="4" y="3" width="16" height="18" rx="2"/><path d="M8 8h8M8 12h8M8 16h5"/></svg></span><span class="fm-lbl">{% t %}A list you upload{% endt %}</span></button>
        <button type="button" class="fm-in" data-step="in"><span class="fm-ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><circle cx="9" cy="8" r="3.5"/><path d="M2.5 20c.8-3.6 3.4-5.5 6.5-5.5s5.7 1.9 6.5 5.5"/><circle cx="17" cy="9" r="2.5"/><path d="M17 14c2.4 0 4 1.5 4.5 4"/></svg></span><span class="fm-lbl">{% t %}People you know{% endt %}</span></button>
        <button type="button" class="fm-in" data-step="in"><span class="fm-ic"><svg viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="1.7" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M4 5h16v11H9l-5 4z"/><path d="M8 9h8M8 12h5"/></svg></span><span class="fm-lbl">{% t %}An inbound lead{% endt %}</span></button>
        </div>
        <div class="fm-bus" aria-hidden="true"><span class="v"></span><span class="h"></span><span class="v"></span></div>
        <button type="button" class="fm-hub is-on" data-step="hub"><b><i><svg viewBox="0 0 12 12" fill="none" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M2 6C2 3.79 3.79 2 6 2s4 1.79 4 4-1.79 4-4 4" stroke="white" stroke-width="1.5" stroke-linecap="round"/><circle cx="6" cy="6" r="1.2" fill="white"/></svg></i>Prospektor</b><span>{% t %}Scores the fit · names who decides · writes the first email{% endt %}</span></button>
        <div class="fm-bus" aria-hidden="true"><span class="v"></span><span class="h bot"></span><span class="v"></span></div>
        <p class="fm-cap">{% t %}Your CRM{% endt %}</p>
        <div class="fm-row crm">
          {%- for c in [['hubspot', 'HubSpot'], ['attio', 'Attio'], ['close', 'Close'], ['affinity', 'Affinity'], ['lightfield', 'Lightfield'], ['reevo', 'Reevo'], ['highlevel', 'HighLevel']] %}
          <a class="fm-out" data-step="crm" href="{{ ('/integrations/' + c[0] + '/') | localize }}"><span class="fm-ic"><img src="{{ ('/assets/img/integrations/' + c[0] + '.svg') | asset }}" alt="" width="22" height="22"></span><span class="fm-lbl">{{ c[1] }}</span></a>
          {%- endfor %}
        </div>
        <p class="fm-foot">{% t %}Your sales process runs there, as it does today.{% endt %}</p>
      </div>
      <aside class="fm-panel">
        <div data-pane="in" hidden>
          <p class="k">{% t %}1 · Where leads come from{% endt %}</p>
          <h3>{% t %}Start from what you already have{% endt %}</h3>
          <p>{% t %}Prospektor reads your website and asks who you sell to. Point it at your best customers, a competitor, a list from a conference or the people you know, and it finds more companies like them.{% endt %}</p>
          <p class="hint">{% t %}Hover or tap any part of the diagram.{% endt %}</p>
        </div>
        <div data-pane="hub">
          <p class="k">{% t %}2 · Prospektor{% endt %}</p>
          <h3>{% t %}Finds the fit, writes the pitch{% endt %}</h3>
          <p>{% t %}Each company gets a fit score with the reasons, the names of the people who decide, and a first email in your voice. Wins and losses you record sharpen the next one.{% endt %}</p>
          <p class="hint">{% t %}Hover or tap any part of the diagram.{% endt %}</p>
        </div>
        <div data-pane="crm" hidden>
          <p class="k">{% t %}3 · Your CRM{% endt %}</p>
          <h3>{% t %}One press, and it is in your pipeline{% endt %}</h3>
          <p>{% t %}Prospektor writes the company, its people, a deal in your first stage and a note with the fit and the angle. Push again and the same records update. From there your team works the way it always has.{% endt %}</p>
          <a class="lnk" href="{{ '/integrations/' | localize }}">{% t %}All integrations{% endt %} ›</a>
        </div>
      </aside>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
<script src="{{ '/assets/js/flow.js' | asset }}" defer></script>
